@startuml monitored_capture_sequence
' Spectracs — a MONITORED capture, from the Measure click to the PDF on disk.
' Companion to spectracsPy/docs/SPEC_settled_measurement.md §27.12 / §27.13 (as-built 2026-08-17).
' Regenerate:  java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg monitored_capture_sequence.puml

title Spectracs — monitored capture: ONE view object, two surfaces\nSPEC_settled_measurement.md §27.12 / §27.13 (as-built 2026-08-17)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ArrowColor #5A7D8C
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3A5A68
skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #5A5A5A
  FontColor #222222
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B36A00
  BackgroundColor #FFF7E6
  FontColor #333333
}

actor "Operator" as OP
participant "CapturePanel\n(Qt host)" as PANEL #E8F5E9
participant "SpectralWorkflowEngine\n(Qt, app tier)" as ENGINE #E8F5E9
participant "Plugin\n(DevSpectralPlugin)" as PLUGIN #FFE6CC
participant "the monitor:\nMonitorEngine (SDK)\n+ FrameRing (SDK)\n+ ClearingEvaluator (plugin)" as MON #FFE6CC
participant "SAMPLE step\n· EvaluationResult" as STEP #CDE7CE
participant "WorkflowReportBuilder\n+ MatplotlibWorkflowRenderer" as REPORT #EAF2FB

== 1 · does this role get a monitor?  (the ONLY role gate in the whole path) ==

OP -> PANEL : click **Measure** on the Sample step
PANEL -> PANEL : __monitorFor(step, role, frames)
note right of PANEL
  ⛔ role == REFERENCE  -> None
  ⛔ no reference captured yet -> None
  ⇒ None means today's plain burst, unchanged
end note
PANEL -> PLUGIN : createMonitor(reference, mode=PRODUCT, frames)
note right of PLUGIN
  ⭐ COMPOSITION, not inheritance (§10.1a-bis):
  the plugin ASSEMBLES MonitorEngine(ring=FrameRing,
  evaluator=its own ClearingEvaluator) and hands it over.
  ⛔ Nothing calls back INTO the plugin during the run.
  ⚠ `mode` is a HOST argument (§17/D3):
     PRODUCT = stop at the read (the bench / wizard)
     DIAGNOSTIC = keep observing to a fixed 20-min arc
     (diagnostics/settling_run.py). Safe only because
     the answer is LATCHED at the read (§14.6).
end note
PLUGIN -> MON ** : assemble
PLUGIN --> PANEL : monitor  (duck-typed: offer / result)

== 2 · the run — the host pumps, the plugin decides ==

PANEL -> ENGINE : captureMonitoredStep(step, frameProvider, monitor, onRow)
loop until monitor.isFinished()   (cancel = provider returns None)
  ENGINE -> PANEL : frameProvider()
  PANEL --> ENGINE : QImage
  ENGINE -> ENGINE : __frameSpectrum(image)   'the SAME per-frame reduction as the burst path
  ENGINE -> MON : offer(frame, clock())
  MON --> ENGINE : row?
  ENGINE -> PANEL : onRow(row, monitor)   '~2 s throttle: status bar + live spectrum
end
ENGINE -> MON : result()
MON --> ENGINE : MonitorResult

== 3 · ⭐ ONE CONSTRUCTION, ONE HOME  (§27.12) ==

ENGINE -> ENGINE : __attachMonitorViews(step, result)
note right of ENGINE
  ⚠ DUCK-TYPED SEAM, not an SDK method:
  hasattr(plugin, "settlingView") inside a try.
  ⛔ A diagnostic must never break the capture
  it documents — a raise prints one line.
  ⇒ §27.13a: declare it on the SDK base class.
end note
ENGINE -> PLUGIN : settlingView(result.toRecord())
PLUGIN --> ENGINE : TabGroupView\n(shownInReport = True)
ENGINE -> STEP : drop any existing isMonitorView item,\nthen addItem(view)  'REPLACE, never accumulate
ENGINE --> PANEL : result  (result.views = [the SAME object])

== 4 · surface A — the screen ==

PANEL -> PANEL : __showSettlingTab(result)\nQtWorkflowRenderer().render(result.views)
note right of PANEL
  ⭐ Renders the very objects now on the step.
  ⛔ The panel builds NO copy of its own —
  that duplication is what made a report-only
  step look necessary (§27.11).
end note

== 5 · surface B — the paper ==

REPORT -> STEP : getEvaluationResult().getItems()
note right of REPORT
  ⭐ Filed under **Acquisition** — the step's PHASE.
  ⛔ No role, label or step-kind is matched anywhere.
end note
REPORT -> REPORT : keep items where willDrawInReport(item)\n-> visitTabGroup prints only the FLAGGED children
note right of REPORT #C8E6C9
  ✅ FIXED 2026-08-17 (§27.13b / D1)
  isShownInReport is honoured at EVERY depth,
  through one shared predicate. Measured:
  3 pages -> 1 page, 0 curve axes, summary intact.
  ⛔ The filter NEVER prunes the view object —
  the panel renders the SAME TabGroupView (Z1).
  ⭐ D4: a sectioned phase is headed per STEP,
  so this lands under "Sample".
end note
REPORT -> REPORT : pypdf embeds workflow.json\n(carries monitorRecord — the machine half)

== 6 · saved, and re-opened ==

PANEL -> STEP : (on Save) EvaluationResult.syncToColumn()
note over STEP #C8E6C9
  ✅ FIXED 2026-08-17 (§27.13c / D2): isMonitorView
  has a default on ReportableView and round-trips
  through TabGroupView ⇒ a re-measure inside a
  RELOADED run replaces rather than appends.
  ⭐ And the tabs come back on re-open because
  step._view is @reconstructor-transient, so the
  reloaded step falls past the capture branch into
  the passive visitor (§27.13d) — no longer an
  accident: pinned by a test, explained in
  renderStep()'s own comment.
end note

@enduml
